{
  "subtopic_code": "8.2",
  "subtopic_title": "Relative and expected frequencies",
  "topic_number": "8",
  "sections": [
    {
      "source_file": "Probability/1-ProbabilityToolkit.json",
      "source_label": "Relative & Expected Frequency",
      "document_title": "ProbabilityToolkit",
      "pages": [
        {
          "page_number": 11,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Relative frequency"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 3,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "What is relative frequency?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Relative frequency is an estimate of a probability using results from an experiment"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "For a certain number of trials of that experience, the probability of 'success' is:"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "\\frac{\\text{Number of successful outcomes}}{\\text{Total number of trials}}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "If you flip an unfair coin 50 times and it lands on heads 20 times, an estimate for the probability of the coin landing on heads is "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "\\frac{20}{50}"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (its relative frequency)"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "That is the best estimate we can make, given the data we have"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "We do not know the actual probability"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The more trials that are carried out, the more accurate relative frequency becomes"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "It gets closer and closer to the actual probability"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 3,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "When will I be asked to use relative frequency?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Relative frequency is used when theoretical probabilities are unavailable (or not possible to calculate)"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "For example, if you do not know the theoretical probability of being left-handed, you can run an experiment to find an estimate (the relative frequency)"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Sometimes theoretical probabilities are known"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The theoretical probability of a fair coin landing on heads is 0.5"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The theoretical probability of a fair standard six-sided dice landing on a six is "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "\\frac{1}{6}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Relative frequency can be compared to a theoretical probability to test if a situation is fair or biased"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "If 100 flips of the coin give a relative frequency of 0.48 for landing on heads, the coin is likely to be fair"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "The theoretical probability is 0.5 and 0.48 is close to 0.5"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "If 100 flips of the coin give a relative frequency of 0.13 for landing on heads, the coin is likely to be biased (not fair)"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 3,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "What else do I need to know about relative frequency?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Relative frequency assumes that there is an equal chance of success on each trial"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "page_number": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The trials are independent of each other"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "For example, if choosing something out of a bag (a ball, or marble etc), it would need to be replaced each time to use relative frequency"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Any experiments used to calculate relative frequency should be random"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "If the experiment is not random, this could introduce bias"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 3,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Examiner Tips and Tricks"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "If you have to choose the best estimate, choose the one with the most trials."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 3,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Worked Example"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "There are an unknown number of different coloured buttons in a bag."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Johan selects a button at random, notes its colour and replaces the button in the bag. Repeating this 30 times, Johan notes that on 18 occasions he selected a red button."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Use Johan's results to estimate the probability that a button drawn at random from the bag is red."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Answer:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Taking 'red' to be a success, Johan had 18 successes out of a total of 30 trials."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\mathrm{P}(\\text{red}) = \\frac{18}{30} = \\frac{3}{5}",
              "display": true,
              "needs_review": true
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 1,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Expected frequency"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "What is expected frequency?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Expected frequency refers to the number of times you would expect a particular outcome to occur"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "It is found by multiplying the probability by the number of trials"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "If you flip a fair coin 100 times, you would expect "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "0.5 \\times 100 = 50"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " heads"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Sometimes you need to calculate the relative frequency first"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "If you flip a biased coin 40 times and get 10 heads, how many heads would you expect when flipping 100 times?"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "The relative frequency is "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "\\frac{10}{40} = 0.25"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " from the first experiment"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "0.25 \\times 100 = 25"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": ", you would expect to get heads 25 times from 100 throws"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "page_number": 13,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Examiner Tips and Tricks"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Exam questions will not necessarily use the phrase \"expected frequency\", but might ask how many you \"would expect\"."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Worked Example"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "There are 6 blue, 4 red and 5 yellow counters in a bag."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "One counter is drawn at random and its colour noted."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The counter is then returned to the bag."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(a) Find the probability that a counter drawn from the bag is yellow."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Answer:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "There are 5 yellow counters out of a total of "
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "6 + 4 + 5 = 15"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " counters in the bag"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\text{P(Yellow)} = \\frac{5}{15} = \\frac{1}{3}",
              "display": true,
              "needs_review": true
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(b) How many times would you expect a yellow counter to be drawn, if this experiment is repeated 300 times?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Answer:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This is expected frequency so multiply the number of trials by the probability from part (a)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "300 \\times \\frac{1}{3} = 100",
              "display": true,
              "needs_review": true
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "We would expect 100 yellow counters"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}